From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps pick colours and set the wallpaper

Two more desktop portals for the NickelOS backend
(xdg-desktop-portal-nickel), on VmApplicationsService:

- NickelPickColor() -> (picked, ARGB): the Screenshot portal's PickColor
  (colour pickers in GIMP, Inkscape, Krita, design and paint apps).
  ChromeOS's eyedropper, the one web pages' colour inputs use
  (components/eye_dropper), on the screen the pointer is on, over
  everything, Linux apps included; a click picks, Esc cancels; one pick at
  a time.
- NickelSetWallpaper(path) -> (done): the Wallpaper portal (GNOME's Image
  Viewer's "Set as Background", wallpaper apps). The picture becomes the
  signed-in user's wallpaper, filling the screen, as Wallpaper & style's
  "My images" sets one (WallpaperController::SetCustomWallpaper keeps its
  own copy); an empty path brings back the default wallpaper.

